Create a .gitignore file for a Python reinforcement learning project with the following entries:

## Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

## Virtual environment
venv/
.venv/
.venv_cuda/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

## Training outputs
checkpoints/
checkpoints_multiseat/
checkpoints_strong/
checkpoints_competitive/
checkpoints_post_selfplay/
train_multiseat.lock
train_strong.lock
*_conflicted_*
graphs/
graphs_multiseat/
graphs_strong/
graphs_competitive/
rewards.csv
rewards_multiseat.csv
rewards_strong.csv
rewards_competitive.csv
rewards_post_selfplay.csv
winrate.csv
winrate_multiseat.csv
winrate_strong.csv
winrate_competitive.csv
winrate_post_selfplay.csv
benchmarks.csv
benchmark_games.csv
benchmarks_multiseat.csv
benchmark_games_multiseat.csv
benchmarks_*_large.csv
benchmark_games_*_large.csv
strong_checkpoint_scores.csv
competitive_checkpoint_scores.csv
post_selfplay_checkpoint_scores.csv
train_post_selfplay.lock
train_competitive.lock
replays/
fresh_start.flag
*.png
*.tar.gz

## PyTorch
*.pth
*.pt

# Published model registry is intentionally tracked with Git LFS
!published_models/
!published_models/*.pth
!published_models/MODEL_REGISTRY.md

## Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb

## IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

## Logs
*.log
logs/
*.out
*.err

## Python packaging / build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
